				<r3d:description language="eng">The Met Office is the UK&#039;s National Weather Service.
We have a long history of weather forecasting and have been working in the area of climate change for more than two decades.
As a world leader in providing weather and climate services, we employ more than 1,800 at 60 locations throughout the world. We are recognised as one of the world&#039;s most accurate forecasters, using more than 10 million weather observations a day, an advanced atmospheric model and a high performance supercomputer to create 3,000 tailored forecasts and briefings a day. These are delivered to a huge range of customers from the Government, to businesses, the general public, armed forces, and other organisations.</r3d:description>
